      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early Bellamy featured a commissary, post office, and modest housing clustered around the mill to support workers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bellamy_alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Allison Lumber Company built Sumter County's first hospital in Bellamy and a multi‑purpose frame building that served as school and church.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bellamy_alabama",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Allison led the town toward selective logging, reforestation, and wildlife protection, hosting annual hunts that drew state politicians in the 1920s.",
